 tri(n) = 1 + n / 2, if n is even.\n    tri(n) =  tri(n - 1) + tri(n - 2) + tri(n + 1), if n is odd.\n    For example:\n    tri(2) = 1 + (2 / 2) = 2\n    tri(4) = 3\n    tri(3) = tri(2) + tri(1) + tri(4)\n           = 2 + 3 + 3 = 8 \n    You are given a non-negative integer number n, you have to a return a list of the \n    first n + 1 numbers of the Tribonacci sequence.\n    Examples:\n    tri(3) = [1, 3, 2, 8]\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _get_tribonacci_term(k):\n        \"\"\"Recursively calculates the k-th Tribonacci number, using memoization.\"\"\"\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        if k == 0:\n            result = 1\n        elif k == 1:\n            result = 3\n        elif k % 2 == 0:  # k is even\n            result = 1 + k // 2\n        else:  # k is odd\n            result = (\n                _get_tribonacci_term(k - 1)\n                + _get_tribonacci_term(k - 2)\n                + _get_tribonacci_term(k + 1)\n            )\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    # The problem statement implies n is non-negative.\n    # If n were negative, an empty list would be a reasonable return per general practice.\n    \n    sequence = []\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        sequence.append(_get_tribonacci_term(i))\n    return sequence", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "pass", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": []}], "HumanEval/139": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/139", "solution": "_factorial_memo = {0: 1, 1: 1}\ndef _factorial(k):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the standard factorial of k using memoization.\"\"\"\n    if k not in _factorial_memo:\n        _factorial_memo[k] = k * _factorial(k - 1)\n    return _factorial_memo[k]\ndef special_factorial(n):\n    \"\"\"The Brazilian factorial is defined as:\n    brazilian_factorial(n) = n! * (n-1)! * (n-2)! * ... * 1!\n    where n > 0\n\n    For example:\n    >>> special_factorial(4)\n    288\n\n    The function will receive an integer as input and should return th